{"availability":"available","full":"Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom","name":"meridian-mailroom","description":"AI mail-triage pipeline for a disability law firm: classify, extract, fuzzy-match, route, with a human gate. Live demo, synthetic data.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-16T12:45:04Z","updated":"2026-07-16T16:31:38Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://meridian-mailroom.vercel.app","topics":["ai","anthropic","automation","document-classification","legal-tech","nextjs"],"demo":"https://meridian-mailroom.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.399Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.399Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.399Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.399Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An AI mail-triage pipeline for a disability law firm, shown as a working internal tool. Incoming scanned mail is classified, has its identifiers extracted, is fuzzy-matched to the right client, and is routed automatically, except for high-stakes letters, which are held for a human before anything happens to them.","Live demo: Everything here is synthetic. Fictional firm, fictional agency, invented people, no real client data.","Law firms drown in mail. A disability practice gets denials, award notices, hearing notices, exam appointments, records requests, and overpayment letters, hundreds a week, each of which has to be read, filed under the right client and matter, and acted on before a deadline slips. This is the pattern I build for that problem, reduced to its architecture and rebuilt on synthetic data so it can be shown in public."],"features":["A human-review gate that fires before any action. Denials, awards, appeal","Fuzzy matching that survives OCR. Scanned mail is full of typos. \"R0bert Castiilo\"","An append-only audit log. Every run and every review decision writes one immutable"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"118e1fe09cf5a1426fded6a00c429282acf627eb8ea39bcafd55e749280f1af2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.532Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.532Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An AI mail-triage pipeline for a disability law firm, shown as a working internal tool. Incoming scanned mail is classified, has its identifiers extracted, is fuzzy-matched to the right client, and is routed automatically, except for high-stakes letters, which are held for a human before anything happens to them.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"row with real token counts and durations, the trail you need for reconciliation and cost tracking.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"118e1fe09cf5a1426fded6a00c429282acf627eb8ea39bcafd55e749280f1af2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.533Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-16T16:31:38Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Drew-Opexcell/meridian-mailroom/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:30.533Z","hash":"118e1fe09cf5a1426fded6a00c429282acf627eb8ea39bcafd55e749280f1af2","originalBytes":5269,"storedBytes":5269,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["real","lib","demo","letters","live","run","what","api","audit","firm","key","letter","one","pipeline","read","review","before","claude","client","damerau-levenshtein","deployment","does","everything","fuzzy","gate","mail","match","matcher","model","npm","recorded","runs","scanned","system","which","about","after","anthropic","any","anything","classify","counts","data.","deadlines","denials","deterministic","disabili